  <p>The Operator bears no liability whatsoever for any damages incurred by users in connection with the use of the Service. The Operator disclaims all liability for damages, including those arising from intentional misconduct or gross negligence of the Operator or persons assisting performance, service outages, natural disasters, storage deletion, data loss, lost authentication information, or unauthorized access and hacking by third parties.</p>
  <p>The Service is provided on an “AS-IS” and “AS-AVAILABLE” basis. The Operator does not warrant that the Service will be error-free, uninterrupted, complete, or fit for a particular purpose. Users assume all risks and liabilities arising from their use of the Service.</p>
  <h2>Article 14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>These Terms are interpreted under the laws of the Republic of Korea, without excluding protections under mandatory provisions applicable to users. The parties will discuss disputes in good faith. If litigation is necessary, a claim may be brought before the competent court determined by applicable law, including the Civil Procedure Act.</p>
  <h2>Article 15. Operator information and contact</h2>
  <p>Miroven is operated personally by Choi Seung-woo (최승우) without business registration. Choi Seung-woo is both the Operator and the person responsible for personal information protection. Send questions about these Terms, objections to restrictions, account deletion requests, and privacy rights requests to <a href="mailto:miroven@mksdr.bid">miroven@mksdr.bid</a>. Include the type of inquiry and relevant account email. Do not send PINs, recovery codes, encryption keys, or plaintext records. The Operator will reply with the outcome after the minimum necessary identity verification.</p>
  <h2>Supplementary provision</h2>
  <p>These Terms take effect on October 25, 2026. Subsequent changes will display an effective date and a summary of changes, and previous versions and their periods of application will remain available.</p>
